    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Project Title: TweakStudio - Conversational IPA Modder\n\nRole & Purpose:\nYou are an expert full-stack developer and iOS security researcher. Build a full-stack web application that allows users to upload a decrypted iOS application (.ipa), converse with an AI agent to design modifications, and automatically generate and inject a Theos-based tweak into the app.\n\nTech Stack:\n\nFrontend: React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.\n\nBackend: Node.js (Server-side runtime with child_process execution capabilities).\n\nAI Integration: Gemini API for the interactive chat agent.\n\nCore User Flow:\n\nUpload & Analyze: Present a clean, drag-and-drop zone for .ipa files. When uploaded, the backend extracts the payload and simulates parsing the app\'s binary headers to build context (mock the class-dump extraction logic for this prototype).\n\nThe Chat Interface: Launch a responsive, split-pane layout once the file is loaded.\n\nLeft Pane: A conversational AI chat interface.\n\nRight Pane: A live code editor displaying the generated Tweak.x or Tweak.swift file.\n\nConversational Tweaking: The user prompts the chat (e.g., \"Hook the main view controller and disable the jailbreak detection check\"). The AI responds with a brief explanation and automatically writes/updates the code in the right pane using standard Logos syntax (%hook, %orig, %end).\n\nBuild & Inject: Provide a prominent \"Compile & Inject\" button. When clicked, the backend simulates the compilation of the tweak via theos and the injection of the .dylib into the binary using tools like optool or Azule, finally presenting a download link for the modified .ipa.\n\nObviuolsy make sure the integrated chat bot has access to the decompiled IPA and can run commands on it to see whats going on and make better tweaks instead of just guessing\n\n\nUI/UX Vibe:\n\nSleek, dark-mode aesthetic suited for development and security research.\n\nThe chat interface should feel snappy, maintaining the history and context of all requested tweaks.\n\nUse a monospaced font for the code editor pane with proper syntax highlighting for Objective-C++ and Swift.\n\nEmbedded AI Agent Rules (How the chat bot should behave):\n\nThe chat agent must act as a veteran iOS tweak developer.\n\nIt must only output code relevant to mobile substrate/Theos hooking.\n\nIf a user asks for a modification that is strictly server-side (like changing database values), the agent must gently correct them and suggest a client-side UI manipulation or memory hook instead.\n\nEdge Cases & State Management:\n\nShow a visually distinct loading state (spinners or skeletons) while the IPA is processing and while the tweak is compiling.\n\nThe chat must handle iterative feedback flawlessly. If the user says, \"Actually, change that boolean to false instead of true,\" the agent should intelligently update the existing hook in the editor pane rather than writing a duplicate hook block."
    items {
      text: "Project Title: TweakStudio - Conversational IPA Modder\n\nRole & Purpose:\nYou are an expert full-stack developer and iOS security researcher. Build a full-stack web application that allows users to upload a decrypted iOS application (.ipa), converse with an AI agent to design modifications, and automatically generate and inject a Theos-based tweak into the app.\n\nTech Stack:\n\nFrontend: React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.\n\nBackend: Node.js (Server-side runtime with child_process execution capabilities).\n\nAI Integration: Gemini API for the interactive chat agent.\n\nCore User Flow:\n\nUpload & Analyze: Present a clean, drag-and-drop zone for .ipa files. When uploaded, the backend extracts the payload and simulates parsing the app\'s binary headers to build context (mock the class-dump extraction logic for this prototype).\n\nThe Chat Interface: Launch a responsive, split-pane layout once the file is loaded.\n\nLeft Pane: A conversational AI chat interface.\n\nRight Pane: A live code editor displaying the generated Tweak.x or Tweak.swift file.\n\nConversational Tweaking: The user prompts the chat (e.g., \"Hook the main view controller and disable the jailbreak detection check\"). The AI responds with a brief explanation and automatically writes/updates the code in the right pane using standard Logos syntax (%hook, %orig, %end).\n\nBuild & Inject: Provide a prominent \"Compile & Inject\" button. When clicked, the backend simulates the compilation of the tweak via theos and the injection of the .dylib into the binary using tools like optool or Azule, finally presenting a download link for the modified .ipa.\n\nObviuolsy make sure the integrated chat bot has access to the decompiled IPA and can run commands on it to see whats going on and make better tweaks instead of just guessing\n\n\nUI/UX Vibe:\n\nSleek, dark-mode aesthetic suited for development and security research.\n\nThe chat interface should feel snappy, maintaining the history and context of all requested tweaks.\n\nUse a monospaced font for the code editor pane with proper syntax highlighting for Objective-C++ and Swift.\n\nEmbedded AI Agent Rules (How the chat bot should behave):\n\nThe chat agent must act as a veteran iOS tweak developer.\n\nIt must only output code relevant to mobile substrate/Theos hooking.\n\nIf a user asks for a modification that is strictly server-side (like changing database values), the agent must gently correct them and suggest a client-side UI manipulation or memory hook instead.\n\nEdge Cases & State Management:\n\nShow a visually distinct loading state (spinners or skeletons) while the IPA is processing and while the tweak is compiling.\n\nThe chat must handle iterative feedback flawlessly. If the user says, \"Actually, change that boolean to false instead of true,\" the agent should intelligently update the existing hook in the editor pane rather than writing a duplicate hook block."
    }
  }
}
