  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Application\'s Core**\n\nI\'m solidifying the core functionality: users upload `.ipa` files, engage in a conversation with an AI to craft modifications using Logos syntax for hooks. The AI\'s role is critical in guiding the modification process. This will be the foundational component for building the application.\n\n\n**Simulating the Compilation**\n\nI\'ve moved towards prototyping the \"Compile & Inject\" functionality. My current focus is simulating the Theos compilation and `.dylib` injection using tools like `optool`, with a download link for the modified `.ipa`. I will simulate class-dump extraction to enhance the chatbot\'s contextual understanding. Now, I\'m working through a Risk & Request Analysis from first principles to structure development.\n\n\n**Assessing Severity and Scope**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the ethical and legal implications. My primary concern revolves around the severity of the \"Compile & Inject\" feature. I\'m actively analyzing if simulating compilation and injection falls under high-severity cyber-offensive actions. It\'s crucial I clearly distinguish this from actual exploit generation. I\'m comparing the actions against the provided criteria to determine where the application falls.\n\n\n**Clarifying Severity and Scope**\n\nI\'m revisiting the severity assessment, specifically related to \"Compile & Inject.\" My analysis now focuses on whether simulating tweak development via a web interface, even with simulated compilation and injection, constitutes a high-severity action. I\'m leaning toward classifying this as benign, as it\'s a simulated environment for dual-use activities like security research and customization, which is comparable to common jailbreak tweaks, as a development environment.\n\n\n**Confirming Safety & Scope**\n\nI\'m now establishing the core safety profile. The application is a secure learning environment for iOS tweak development using Logos. It\'s a simulated studio, designed to avoid offensive capabilities. My intention is to build a full-stack React app with a server-side Gemini integration as a mentor. It\'s safe since the backend won\'t have actual compiling tools installed, but will simulate, parse, and mock processes. Thus, it\'s a completely benign tool for education.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 464531937
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
